    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1236">

                <pb facs="1281" n="1269" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/11–245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Assistant Chief of
                        the Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jones</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-11-02">November 2, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At my request Mr. Eralp<anchor n="87a" xml:id="d1236-f1"/> called at 10:30 a.m.
                    today. I handed him the text of the note delivered by Ambassador Wilson to the
                    Turkish Minister for Foreign Affairs at 3:30 p.m., November 2.</p>
                <p>Mr. Eralp read the note and smiled broadly. He said that in his opinion it was
                    “very satisfactory” and that “Turkey could have hoped for nothing better.”</p>
                <p>A copy of the communication handed to Mr. Eralp is attached.<anchor n="87b"
                        xml:id="d1236-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1236-f1" n="87a" xml:id="d1236-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Orhan Eralp, Second Secretary, Turkish Embassy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1236-f2" n="87b" xml:id="d1236-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram 1049, October 30, 3 p.m., <ref target="#pg1265">p. 1265</ref>.</p>
            </note>
